  "rationale": "With no mitigations, rce_achieved is reachable through one path: inject_jndi_string -> trigger_jndi_lookup -> resolve_to_attacker -> return_malicious_reference -> load_class_via_gadget -> execute_payload. The alternative load_class_via_reference is already blocked because trust_url_codebase=false. The only remaining class-loading step is load_class_via_gadget, so the attack is a single chain. Breaking any one link stops it, and each of these mitigations does that alone: input_validation, formatMsgNoLookups, remove_jndi_class, disable_jndi, block_egress or remove_gadget. trust_url_codebase_false adds nothing. No mitigations is not enough because rce is reachable, so the minimum is 1. This assumes each mitigation disables the configuration condition its name refers to; the model's wording that a mitigation 'makes its constant true' is ambiguous on this point."
